      "writtenOn": "2017-02-02T00:19:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Returning an error via Bytes() seems pretty reasonable, but do we really want this option? I suspect this code should have a stronger opinion.",
      "revId": "05b575bd92fb82bfa7031ed8900b9cd5b3a18a5a",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "eb683a33_dd8af345",
        "filename": "cryptobyte/builder.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 31,
      "author": {
        "id": 16331
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-02T01:35:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My concern was that getting an error from Bytes() that says \"tried to write 312 bytes with a 1-byte length prefix\", with no way to tell at what point during building the error actually happened, would be painful to debug. Panic-ing would give you a better hint as to where you made a mistake.\n\nIn TLS, any error returned from Bytes() would result in a panic anyway, I assume, so why not crash early?\n\nOTOH, as I think you noted, the current code doesn\u0027t highlight coding errors like that either, i.e. not doing panicOnError is not any worse. So I\u0027m tempted to just take it out.",
      "revId": "05b575bd92fb82bfa7031ed8900b9cd5b3a18a5a",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": false
    },
